
# EXPERIMENT NO. 1.1
# Design and Draft the Given 2D Sketches in Modelling Software

---

## AIM

To draft a 2D sketch in the software.
<img width="632" height="566" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8bdfbb2c-b013-442d-bea4-846211667217" />


## MATERIALS REQUIRED

1. AutoCAD Fusion 360
2. Windows 10
3. 16GB RAM (integrated graphics recommend 1GB or more)

---

## PROCEDURE

1. Open a new file and then select the sketch icon.

2. Select the plane for sketching.

3. Use sketching features in the Create option (line, circle, arc, rectangle, polygon, etc.).
<img width="421" height="150" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e76d3d88-a25a-475a-ac9e-8dbb6bbe6dc0" />

4. Use the Modify features to bring details to your sketch.
<img width="411" height="165" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bf99bb8f-99a4-4652-9ecb-cfa666c3318d" />

5. Use the Constraint feature to finish the sketch and specify dimensions.
<img width="462" height="140" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/118e40e1-7295-4608-91a6-8325726dfe5d" />

6. After finishing the sketch, use the Finish Sketch option to finalise the diagram.
<img width="380" height="252" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a0b3b5f-2f09-4c37-ad82-d1368c9e884d" />

7. Switch to Drawing mode to plot the sketch in ISO standard.

<img width="520" height="301" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/97e4373e-c7e1-4cdd-b7eb-a1bc03091134" />


